  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": 0,
      "title": "Method details",
      "instruction": "A reproducible data preparation process was designed to transform an original dataset of 23 variables into a dataset ready for use in modeling with machine learning algorithms while preserving its clinical meaning.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 1,
      "title": "Method details",
      "instruction": "The process is divided into two stages: data collection and data preprocessing. The latter has the following steps: depersonalization, variable elimination, handling of multi-valued variables, variable transformation, correction of inconsistencies, handling of missing values, duplicate removal, and outlier detection (Fig. 1).Fig. 1Method to transform the original hospital dataset (23 variables) into a modeling-ready resource (16 variables).Fig 1",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 2,
      "title": "Method validation",
      "instruction": "In this section, we empirically validate how the preprocessing workflow not only improves data quality for modeling with machine learning algorithms but also adds value by more accurately reflecting real clinical characteristics and ensuring reproducibility beyond a single performance metric such as accuracy.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    }
  ],
